From e7f5b3c2caaf2f2396e0811519fc7fdae78f2a3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Murgola <admin@murgo.la>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:08:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] moe: register the RAM tier with the GPU, so its experts
 upload by DMA

The locked --moe-ram-mib ranges are registered with the first backend that pins host memory (a new ungated
ggml_backend_register_host_range in the CUDA backend), the most used experts first up to --moe-ram-register-mib
(default 40% of physical RAM: the Windows display driver backs registrations past about half of RAM with device
memory), page-rounded and merged where they touch. Cache misses that fall in a registered range are queued on the
backend's stream straight from the mapping instead of going through the stager's copy threads: 47 GB/s against
16 GB/s measured on a 5090 over PCIe 5.0. The cache stats line shows the direct bytes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KoGLukxXjcjdP8MU4HWp46
